From 4194f7c51bf0042212e7fda346ab71a8521f6a41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:36:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] components, v4l2: MPEG-4 Part 2 and H.263

Add c2.v4l2.mpeg4.{decoder,encoder} and c2.v4l2.h263.{decoder,encoder},
enabled with the vendor properties
ro.vendor.v4l2_codec2.{decoder,encoder}.supported.{mpeg4,h263} like the
other codecs, for stateful V4L2 devices (V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG4 and
V4L2_PIX_FMT_H263; there is no stateless API for them):

- VideoCodec::MPEG4 and H263, their profiles, levels and pixel formats.
  MPEG-4 profiles and levels are queried from the device; H.263 has no
  V4L2 control for either, so Baseline and levels 10 to 70 are assumed.
- Decoder: a key frame is a VOL header or an intra VOP for MPEG-4, an
  intra picture for H.263; output delay of 8, as for VP8.
- Encoder: MPEG-4 Simple only (no B-frames, so Advanced Simple brings
  nothing), levels 0 to 5, maximum QP 31, headers joined with the first
  frame; the VOS, VO and VOL headers in front of the first VOP are the
  codec config data. H.263 Baseline, maximum QP 31, no codec config data.

Tested on Exynos7870 (s5p-mfc): MPEG-4 Simple 720p and 1278x718 and
H.263 QCIF and CIF decoded identical to ffmpeg, frame by frame; MPEG-4
Simple 720p and 1080p and H.263 CIF, 4CIF and 720p encoded from buffers
and from a Surface, decoded by ffmpeg without errors.

